    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d36">

                <pb facs="0143" n="51" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg51"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/1221b</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d36-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-29T20:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 29, 1918, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6383. It has been reported in the press that Count
                        Czernin stated to the Austrian Delegations that the text of his
                    recent speech had already been submitted to President Wilson before being delivered. <pb facs="0144" n="52"
                        xml:id="pg52"/> You may informally advise the Government to which you are
                    accredited that there is no foundation whatever for this statement. At the same
                    time you may state that in view of the apparent sensation which the statement is
                    causing in Germany, the Department is not making any comment for publication at
                    the present time. Repeat to Paris, 3117, and Rome, 1050.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d36-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d36-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated by circular telegram, on the same date, “for your information and not
                    for communication,” to the diplomatic representatives in Denmark, Greece (for
                    paraphrase to the Special Agent at Corfu), the Netherlands, Norway, Portugal,
                    Russia, Spain, Sweden, and Switzerland.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
